WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
In Egypt, at Giza,
stands the Great Sphinx.

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:08.290
It was carved from a rock ridge,
but perhaps not from scratch.

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:14.130
A USGS publication suggests the Sphinx
may have begun as a natural landform.

4
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.830
Nature may have shaped the ridge first.

5
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.890
So what can shape a
rock ridge in a desert,

6
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.310
long before anyone picks up a tool?

7
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:26.790
In this mission, you'll see how a desert
surface can be stripped down to a pavement

8
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.270
of stones.

9
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.530
Then you'll trace how desert
landscapes change on every time-scale,

10
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.110
from a few seconds to
whole glacial cycles.

11
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.350
Your mission: find out what shaped the
rock ridge the Great Sphinx was carved

12
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:40.910
from.
